# Structure transcripts without hiding uncertainty

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical domain evidence does not imply a working adapter. The finite
contract preserves explicit unavailable capabilities.

Turn reviewed transcript spans into sections, definitions, examples, and
formulas while retaining time ranges, confidence, speakers, and unresolved text.

Current executable evidence now freezes an evidence-preserving reviewed-span
boundary without choosing a structuring algorithm. Section, Definition, Example,
Formula, and Unresolved roles remain caller-reviewed classifications linked to
the complete source transcript. Review now rejects resolved-word slices or
unresolved-fragment references borrowed from a different transcript instead of
relabeling them under the supplied transcript provenance. Empty resolved-word
slices also fail as unverifiable because they contain no addressable word
evidence that can prove source membership.

Resolved spans retain original word timing, confidence, speaker, and text
evidence; explicit unresolved fragments retain their text, timing, and
confidence and cannot be silently promoted to a confident role. A 10-state
role/source oracle crosses all five reviewed roles with resolved-word and
unresolved-fragment evidence: every role may retain resolved evidence, while
only `Unresolved` may retain an unresolved fragment. Each admitted review span
also retains an exact source address: a half-open range of resolved words or an
unresolved-fragment index in the supplied transcript. Overlapping and repeated
reviewed spans remain valid because source addressing does not choose
segmentation.

The validated structure is constructor-owned and exposes read-only transcript,
span, and location views so callers cannot forge span/location alignment. Span
segmentation, role selection, transcript correction, confidence policy, semantic
notebook construction, and layout remain open.

## Finite reviewed timed transcript organization contract

**Inputs:** one immutable source-linked transcript with original timed words,
optional speaker IDs, confidence evidence and unresolved fragments, plus one
user-reviewed role assignment. **Outputs:** a read-only ordered structure
candidate with `Section`, `Definition`, `Example`, `Formula`, or `Unresolved`
roles linked to exact source ranges; no accepted notebook mutation.

**Worked 20-second fragment:** words at `0..4 s`, speaker A, contain
`Energy is work over time`; the reviewer labels the range a `Definition`.
Words `5..9 s` contain `For example one joule per second` and become
`Example`. A low-confidence fragment from `10..13 s` remains
`Unresolved` with original time/confidence rather than invented equation
symbols. Words `14..20 s` explain `P equals E divided by t`; a reviewer
may propose `Formula` only while preserving the exact spoken words as
source evidence and separately verifying symbol semantics.

**Review rule:** retain source clip ID, exact half-open word ranges or
unresolved-fragment index, speaker when established, original token text,
time and confidence. Unknown speaker remains `UnknownSpeaker`; unknown
speech remains unresolved. A corrected transcript is a new version with
linked original evidence, not a silent replacement. Overlapping ranges
are permitted only when their source addresses remain unambiguous.

**Refusal example:** an unresolved audio interval is assigned a confident
`Formula`, a timestamp is outside the media duration, a source range is
missing, or a speaker is invented. Return typed invalid review without
constructing notebook blocks. No summarizer may claim semantic correctness
from word timing alone or discard the uncertainty to fit a page.

**Assumptions and limits:** typed reviewed span roles, source addresses and
constructor-sealed evidence exist. Real transcript correction, role
classification, notebook construction, timing checks against decoded media
and rendering remain unimplemented. This example is theoretical media text.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for role/address preservation; theoretical for
  full reviewed media pipeline, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one timed fragment with definition/example/formula and
  unresolved interval, source/speaker retention and invalid-role refusal.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** actual audio recognition,
  semantic structuring algorithm, correction UI or rendered content.
